{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-11 10:47:28 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 17:47:28 +07\nCoding-Agent: muse\nSession-ID: 7db9b5cc-3472-4c31-9657-1b41aaa76ae3\nModel: muse-wonder-1.0\n\n# cc3 fix round r5 — F2 caller threading, F6 maximum rule, bounded run v2: findings\n\nStatus: COMPLETE — all three r5 items fixed and verified in the\nuncommitted eight-file diff on `cc3-lowering-provenance` (base\n`ced9f2c2`; 8 files, +1620/−93 at delivery). Nothing committed. The r5\nchanges touch one of the eight tracked files\n(`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`, F2), the in-repo measurement\nscript (`collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj`, F6),\nthe r4 findings table (one verdict cell corrected, samples\nunchanged), and the NEW v2 declaration\n(`collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md`).\nNo forbidden file was edited; F1/F3/F4/F5 areas were not touched.\nDeliverable note: the requested canonical path under\n`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/` is outside\nthis session's writable workspace, so this is the worktree mirror at\n`collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md`\nin `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3` — copy it (and the v2\ndeclaration mirror beside it) to the canonical collab path from a\nshell with write access there.\n\n## Item 1 — F2 residue: scope threaded through the ACTUAL callers — FIXED\n\n- New run composition: `fresh-admission-run` (latte_oracle_test.clj)\n  allocates ONE admission run — a fresh scope supplied as plain data\n  (`\"<label>-<UUID>\"`) plus a run-local ordinal allocator (an atom\n  created per run, held only by the run map; no per-JVM global\n  counter). `kernel-compile-in-run` / `kernel-row-in-run` thread that\n  run through the actual callers, assigning DISTINCT ordinals within\n  the run. Replay never allocates a fresh run: it explicitly\n  re-supplies the retained run's scope+ordinal, or reuses the\n  retained compilation (the pre-existing binding-replay pin).\n- `kernel-row` now takes `[fixture run-scope admission-ordinal]`\n  (the old always-`:kernel-row 0` call is gone) and records\n  `:admission-origin` / `:admission-scope` / `:admission-ordinal` on\n  the row; the evidence writer dissocs those three when landing the\n  versioned evidence file, so generated evidence stays stable across\n  fresh scopes. `kernel-gate-evidence` — the run composition of the\n  evidence run — allocates its scope ONCE and threads it through\n  every fixture row via `kernel-row-in-run`.\n- Every other caller updated: the proof-supply doseq, the proof-loop\n  doseq, and check-proof (one `fresh-admission-run` per testing\n  block, distinct ordinals per iteration); the principal binding\n  test (allocates its enclosing `:cc3-binding-run` identity once,\n  compiles as its ordinal-0 admission, and pins\n  `[(:scope run) 0]` as the origin's batch token); the duplicate-id\n  test; `test-kernel-unused-arity-execution`; the h3-2 and h3-3\n  families; and the attribution battery (one run threaded through\n  all its rows, including the nested case-3/case-6 rows). No\n  `:kernel-row 0`, `:proof-* 0`, `:check-proof 0`, or fixed\n  `:cc3-binding-run 0` coordinate remains.\n- Pin through the ACTUAL caller path (new deftest\n  `test-cc3-caller-run-threads-distinct-admissions`): through\n  `kernel-row` itself — identical content admitted twice in one run\n  takes ordinals 0 and 1 under the run's one scope and mints\n  distinct origins; a fresh run supplies a distinct scope, restarts\n  at ordinal 0, and still mints a new origin; explicitly\n  re-supplying the retained scope+ordinal 0 reproduces the first\n  row's origin (replay). Constructor-level pins (distinct scopes,\n  nonzero ordinal, binding replay) remain in\n  `test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins`.\n\n## Item 2 — F6 residue: maximum-based pass/fail — FIXED\n\n- The measurement script's verdict is now maximum-based:\n  `:under-ceilings-v2` compares the MAXIMUM observed sample against\n  each ceiling (retained = max of the compiled-inclusive samples;\n  peak = max over pipeline repetitions; time = max elapsed; storage\n  = max per artifact and max aggregate). Medians are printed only as\n  `:*-median-informational` and never establish compliance.\n- The superseded run's table is corrected honestly: in the r4\n  findings, the binding-only holder's verdict now reads EXCEEDED\n  (the 8,044,024 B sample is over the 8,000,000 B ceiling; the r4\n  median-based \"under (99.5%)\" label was wrong). Its samples are\n  unchanged, and the compiled-inclusive holder remains EXCEEDED.\n  The superseded run stays FAILED — see the v2 declaration §5.\n\n## Item 3 — NEW versioned bounded run (ruling (c)) — DECLARED AND RUN\n\nDeclaration (written BEFORE the v2 run):\n`collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md`\n(worktree mirror) — pinned corpus/revision and host/JVM settings;\nretained object set INCLUDING the compiled input and the binding's\nreconstruction evidence (correspondence, stamped trees/rows/paths),\nmaximum simultaneously retained fixtures = 1; separate finite\nceilings — storage 2,000,000 B per artifact and 4,000,000 B\naggregate, retained memory **12,000,000 B** (above the pilot\ncompiled-inclusive maximum 9,008,912 B by +33.2% stated headroom;\n+34.2% over its 8,939,024 B median; the pilot binding-only maximum\n8,044,024 B also clears it by +49.2%), peak heap 1,073,741,824 B,\ntime 10,000 ms per pipeline repetition, guest instructions / trace\nrecords 4,000,000 / 1,000,000 restated not raised; the exact\nreproducible procedure (compiled-inclusive acceptance variant, 5\nretained repetitions per variant, 3 pipeline repetitions, 2 ms peak\nsampling, sampling limitations, maximum-based pass/fail); and the\nsuperseded run's failed status and both exceedances, without\nrelabelling it successful.\n\nV2 measurement results (2026-11-11, warm JVM, this host/JVM; run\nscope `cc3-f6-measure-v2-ce2fe8c8-2562-4b4a-9326-e51ac82c74e9`; run\ncommand in the declaration §4; both C lanes `:completed` in all 3\npipeline repetitions; after-release GC-used heap 39,313,800 B):\n\n| Quantity | V2 samples (all recorded) | Maximum | V2 ceiling | Verdict (max rule) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Retained: compiled-inclusive holder (acceptance) | 8,913,176 / 8,839,920 / 8,931,952 / 8,825,592 / 8,877,128 B | 8,931,952 B | 12,000,000 B | PASS (74.4% of ceiling) |\n| Retained: binding-only holder (informational) | 8,274,760 / 7,918,496 / 7,918,208 / 7,933,840 / 7,968,320 B | 8,274,760 B | 12,000,000 B | under (informational; not the acceptance holder) |\n| Storage: rows canonical bytes | 312,886 B ×3 | 312,886 B | 2,000,000 B | PASS |\n| Storage: relation canonical bytes | 856,315 B ×3 | 856,315 B | 2,000,000 B | PASS |\n| Storage: durable record canonical bytes | 544 B ×3 | 544 B | — (in aggregate) | — |\n| Storage: aggregate retained set | 1,169,745 B ×3 | 1,169,745 B | 4,000,000 B | PASS |\n| Peak used heap (2 ms sampling) | 253,908,344 / 283,147,736 / 259,288,088 B | 283,147,736 B | 1,073,741,824 B | PASS |\n| Pipeline elapsed | 820 / 873 / 849 ms | 873 ms | 10,000 ms | PASS |\n\nNotes: v2 serialized sizes exceed the r4 pilot's (rows 293,924 →\n312,886 B; relation 802,260 → 856,315 B) because admission origins\nnow carry the longer r5 run-scope strings — inside the declared\nheadroom and recorded, not hidden. Retained-memory method limits are\nunchanged (process-wide used-heap delta, GC-pinned, warm JVM; an\norder-of-magnitude claim comparable only on this host/JVM class,\nnever an object-graph census; 2 ms sampling can miss sub-2 ms\ntransients). The `/tmp/cc3-f6-store-*` file stores from this run\nwere removed after the run.\n\n## Red-first evidence\n\n| Item | Red | Green |\n|---|---|---|\n| F2 caller path | new `test-cc3-caller-run-threads-distinct-admissions` against the unthreaded code: compile error `Unable to resolve symbol: fresh-admission-run` (the run-threading API and row origin did not exist; `kernel-row` still stamped every row `:kernel-row 0`) | 0 failures (see verification; 10 oracle deftests, 230 assertions in the combined affected run) |\n| F6 max rule | n/a — measurement/record fix; the defect is the r4 script's median comparison at its `:retained-aggregate` verdict and the r4 table's \"under\" label, both quoted in astra's r4 confirm | v2 script verdicts are max-based; corrected table above and in the r4 findings |\n\n## Verification\n\n| Lane | Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| Oracle affected deftests (cc3 binding/nested/grammar/distinct + caller-run + proof supply + unused-arity + h3-2 + h3-3 + attribution battery) | `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v …` (10 vars) | 10 tests, 230 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Callsite battery | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 36 tests, 403 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Semantic nets | `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.linearize-test -n yin.vm.semantic.derive-test` | 51 tests, 7,333 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| REPL nets | `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test` | 79 tests, 400 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Kernel gate evidence (actual evidence-run caller path) | `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-gate-evidence-writer-round-trip` | 2 tests, 1,301 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors (`:gate-status :pass`, 155 fixtures) |\n| F6 v2 measurement | declaration §4 command | results table above; all `:under-ceilings-v2` true |\n| kondo (all 8 changed files) | `clj -M:kondo --lint <8 files>` | errors: 0, warnings: 0 |\n\n## Invariants and unchanged items\n\n- Zero canonical change, origins never minted, legacy loadable: the\n  F2 coordinate is still supplied by the admitting composition and\n  recorded as plain data; the scope is now allocated once per run by\n  that composition instead of being a fixed keyword at each caller.\n  No admission global was introduced (the ordinal atom is created\n  per run and held only by the threaded run map).\n- F1/F3/F4/F5: untouched this round; the callsite battery above\n  re-verifies F4's link-resume test.\n- Eight tracked files only; forbidden list unchanged and unedited.\n  Nothing committed.\n\n## Unverified items\n\n- Canonical collab copies of this deliverable and of the v2\n  declaration: write-blocked by this session's sandbox (worktree\n  mirrors carry both texts).\n- Full oracle suite and suite-scale battery: shiva at landing (per\n  the original brief); the affected oracle deftests and the gate\n  evidence tests ran here (see table).\n- cljs/cljd lanes: not run on this laptop; kondo's dual analysis is\n  the evidence (0 errors).\n- Retained-memory method: order-of-magnitude used-heap claim (see\n  limits in Item 3), not an object-graph census.\n- Cold-JVM time ceilings: declared from warm pilot measurements, as\n  §6.3 permits.\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-11 13:40:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 20:40:00 +0700\nCoding-Agent: muse\nSession-ID: 7db9b5cc-3472-4c31-9657-1b41aaa76ae3\n\n# cc3 bounded run declaration v2 — NEW versioned run (astra r4 ruling (c))\n\nThis declaration is written BEFORE the v2 measurement run, per design\n§6.3 and astra's r4 exceedance ruling (c). It creates a NEW, explicitly\nversioned bounded run. It does not amend, re-scope, or relabel the\nsuperseded run (see §5).\n\n## 1. Pinned corpus, revision, host, and JVM settings\n\n| Item | Pinned value |\n|---|---|\n| Worktree / branch | `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`, branch `cc3-lowering-provenance` |\n| Base revision | `ced9f2c2bdb43ab4a416b4ab408c76eb29245764` plus the uncommitted eight-file cc3 diff (+1495/−68 at r4 delivery; latte oracle test file further changed in r5 for F2 caller threading — behaviour-neutral for this fixture's compiled content) |\n| Fixture (the whole corpus of this run) | `{:id :cc3-binding :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` admitted through `kernel-compile`, bound through `cc3-oracle-binding` |\n| Upstream oracle revision | latte-kernel `86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279` (pinned in `deps.edn` `:test` alias) |\n| Compiler base recorded by the evidence harness | `7dc18478` |\n| Host | Darwin 25.6.0 arm64, Apple M1 Pro, 17,179,869,184 B RAM |\n| JVM | OpenJDK 17.0.18+0 (Homebrew, 64-Bit Server VM, mixed mode) |\n| Clojure | Clojure CLI 1.12.4.1602; project `:test` JVM opts `-Xss64m`, no explicit `-Xmx` (JVM default max heap) |\n| Measurement script | `collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj` (in-repo, r5 revision: maximum-based rule, compiled-inclusive holder) |\n\n## 2. Retained object set and maximum simultaneous retention\n\nThe retained set for one fixture, all held simultaneously by one local\nholder (never a global Var), is:\n\n- the **compiled input**: the `kernel-compile` result (compiled AST,\n  stamped AST, site table, retained `:admission-origin`);\n- the **binding**: `cc3-oracle-binding` result (C1 tree, rows, marked\n  and eligible occurrence sets, site→key binding);\n- the **reconstruction evidence**: the binding's stamped tree/rows,\n  stamped marked/eligible sets, site correspondence map, and stamped\n  paths — i.e. everything needed to reconstruct and verify each bound\n  key from the retained compilation;\n- the lowered images: `linearize/project-rows` output plus\n  `derive/stack-image` and `derive/register-image`;\n- the provenance relation (schema-1 map over admission/root and the\n  semantic, stack, and register call-provenance) and, in the pipeline\n  variant, its durable record in a file-backed content store.\n\nTwo holder variants are measured: **binding-only** (binding, lowered\nimages, relation, reconstruction evidence — the compiled input is\nreleased after binding) and **compiled-inclusive** (the same set plus\nthe retained compiled input). The compiled-inclusive variant is the\nacceptance variant; the binding-only variant is reported for\ncomparison and is NOT the acceptance holder.\n\n**Maximum simultaneously retained fixtures: 1.** Every retained and\npeak measurement holds exactly one fixture's retained set at a time;\nthe previous holder is released (and GC-pinned) before the next\nrepetition builds a new one.\n\n## 3. Ceilings (separate, finite, pilot-justified)\n\nPilot measurements (superseded run, r4, warm JVM, same host/JVM):\nbinding-only retained samples 7,960,192 / 7,921,728 / 8,044,024 B\n(median 7,960,192 B, **maximum 8,044,024 B**); compiled-inclusive\nsamples 9,008,912 / 8,939,024 / 8,826,416 B (median 8,939,024 B,\n**maximum 9,008,912 B**); serialized rows 293,924 B; serialized\nrelation 802,260 B; peak used heap 292,720,240 B (GC-pinned baseline\n38,967,336 B); pipeline elapsed 1,727 ms.\n\n| Ceiling | v2 bound | Justification / headroom over pilot |\n|---|---|---|\n| Storage, per artifact (serialized canonical bytes) | **2,000,000 B** | Kept from r2. Pilot rows 293,924 B (6.8× headroom), relation 802,260 B (2.5× headroom). |\n| Storage, aggregate retained serialized set (rows + relation + durable record, 1 fixture) | **4,000,000 B** | Pilot rows+relation = 1,096,184 B; the durable record is a small map over the same data. 4,000,000 B is ≥3.6× the pilot partial sum, leaving room for the record while staying finite. |\n| Retained memory, aggregate (1 fixture, compiled-inclusive holder) | **12,000,000 B** | Set ABOVE the pilot compiled-inclusive **maximum** 9,008,912 B by 2,991,088 B (**+33.2% headroom**; +34.2% over the 8,939,024 B median; +49.2% over the binding-only maximum 8,044,024 B). Pilot repetition spread was ~2% (8,826,416–9,008,912 B), so 33% covers GC-delta noise, the longer r5 run-scope strings (tens of bytes), and host jitter on this machine class, without being an order-of-magnitude loosening. The floor is the measured maximum, per ruling (c): a ceiling at or below 9,008,912 B would declare a run already known to exceed it. |\n| Peak heap (absolute used heap during the pipeline) | **1,073,741,824 B (1 GiB)** | Kept from r2. Pilot peak 292,720,240 B is 27.3% of this ceiling (3.67× headroom); the figure is absolute used heap (baseline + harness + transients), so the margin absorbs sampler/baseline variance. |\n| Time, per pipeline repetition (compile → persistence → both tagged lanes) | **10,000 ms** | Kept from r2. Pilot 1,727 ms gives 5.8× headroom; warm-JVM figure, cold-JVM limits are stated in §4. |\n| Guest instructions / trace records per C lane | **4,000,000 / 1,000,000** | Restated from the r1 record, NOT raised. |\n\n## 4. Exact reproducible measurement procedure\n\nScript: `collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj`\n(r5 revision). Run from the worktree root:\n\n```\nclojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:f6 {:extra-paths [\"test\"] :extra-deps {latte-kernel/latte-kernel {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\" :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}}}}' -M:f6 collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj\n```\n\n(the latte-kernel git dependency is named explicitly because the\nproject's `:test` alias, which normally carries it, also carries the\ntest-runner main opts; the git checkout is already cached locally.\nVerdicts are read from the script's printed `:under-ceilings-v2` map,\ncomputed by the maximum rule below.)\n\nProcedure, in order:\n\n1. **Warmup**: build one retained structure and one full pipeline\n   pass, DISCARD both, GC-pin. Class loading / JIT are charged to the\n   warmup, not to measured repetitions.\n2. **Retained memory**: 5 repetitions per holder variant\n   (binding-only, then compiled-inclusive). Each repetition builds a\n   fresh holder held only by a local, samples GC-pinned used heap\n   (`System/gc()`, 50 ms, `System/gc()`, then\n   `Runtime.totalMemory − freeMemory`) before and after, uses\n   `System/identityHashCode` on the holder AFTER the second sample so\n   it cannot be collected early, and releases it on return. ALL 5\n   samples per variant are recorded.\n3. **Peak / pipeline**: 3 pipeline repetitions. A sampler thread\n   records used heap every 2 ms across lowering → binding /\n   projection / derives → actual serialization\n   (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) → durable persistence\n   (`dao.jing/materialize!` of relation and record into a file-backed\n   `yin.repl.store`, closed) → tagged execution (both C lanes must\n   reach `:completed`). Peak, per-repetition elapsed time, and\n   serialized byte counts are recorded per repetition.\n4. **Pass/fail is MAXIMUM-based** (r5 F6 fix): a ceiling is met only\n   if the MAXIMUM observed value is at or under it — retained memory:\n   max of the 5 compiled-inclusive samples ≤ 12,000,000 B (the\n   binding-only samples are reported, and also max-checked against\n   the same aggregate ceiling for information); storage: max per\n   artifact and max aggregate ≤ their ceilings; peak heap: max peak\n   over the 3 repetitions ≤ 1 GiB; time: max elapsed ≤ 10,000 ms.\n   Any single sample over its ceiling = EXCEEDED. Medians are\n   printed for information only and never establish compliance.\n\nSampling limitations (named, not hidden): retained and peak figures\nare process-wide JVM used-heap values, not an object-graph census;\n`System/gc()` is a hint the JVM honored observably here, not a\nguarantee; 2 ms peak sampling can miss sub-2 ms transients; figures\nare comparable only on this host/JVM class and only for the named\nholder scope; times are warm-JVM (the discarded warmup precedes all\nmeasured repetitions).\n\n## 5. Superseded run: failed status preserved\n\nThe r2/r4 bounded run (8,000,000 B aggregate retained ceiling,\nmedian-based accounting in its r4 record) **FAILED and remains\nfailed**. Its exceedances, restated with maximum-based accounting:\n\n- compiled-inclusive holder: samples 9,008,912 / 8,939,024 /\n  8,826,416 B — every sample over the 8,000,000 B ceiling.\n  **EXCEEDED.**\n- binding-only holder: samples 7,960,192 / 7,921,728 / 8,044,024 B —\n  the 8,044,024 B sample is over the 8,000,000 B ceiling, so under\n  the corrected maximum rule this holder is **EXCEEDED** too (its r4\n  \"under (99.5%)\" median label is corrected in r5; the samples\n  themselves are unchanged).\n\nNothing in this v2 declaration relabels that run successful, raises\nits ceiling retroactively, or shrinks its fixture. The v2 run below\nis a separate, new run under the ceilings in §3; its results are\nrecorded in the r5 findings, not back-written into the superseded\nrun's record.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
