 are derived by yang.latte-oracle-test, so this script and the test\n;; cannot disagree about what a regenerated table holds.\n;; Run: clj -X:test:dev latte-oracle-tables/-main\n(ns latte-oracle-tables\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.pprint :as pp]\n            [yang.latte-oracle-test]))\n\n\n(defn- derived\n  \"The result of calling the oracle test's private derivation `sym`.\"\n  [sym]\n  ((deref (ns-resolve 'yang.latte-oracle-test sym))))\n\n\n(defn- write-table!\n  [file header rows]\n  (io/make-parents file)\n  (spit file (str header (with-out-str (pp/pprint rows))))\n  (println \"wrote\" (count rows) \"rows to\" file))\n\n\n(def ^:private exclusions\n  {'latte_kernel.utils/nano-time \"Reads the host monotonic clock; no portable clock capability is installed.\"\n   'latte_kernel.unparser/show-term \"Captures host output and invokes clojure.pprint; formatting is host-local.\"\n   'latte_kernel.proof/show-term \"Invokes the excluded host pprint/output formatter.\"\n   'latte_kernel.proof/show-def \"Invokes the excluded host pprint/output formatter.\"\n   'latte_kernel.proof/elab-print-term \"Writes directly to host stdout; no portable output stream is supplied.\"\n   'latte_kernel.proof/elab-print-type \"Writes directly to host stdout; no portable output stream is supplied.\"\n   'latte_kernel.proof/elab-print-def \"Writes directly to host stdout; no portable output stream is supplied.\"\n   'latte_kernel.proof/elab-print-defenv \"Writes directly to host stdout; no portable output stream is supplied.\"\n   'latte_kernel.proof/print-state \"Writes directly to host stdout; no portable output stream is supplied.\"})\n\n\n(defn- admission-rows\n  []\n  (mapv (fn [{:keys [ns name] :as row}]\n          (let [excluded (get exclusions (symbol (str ns) (str name)))]\n            (assoc row :source (str (str/replace (str ns) \".\" \"/\") \".cljc\")\n                   :disposition (if excluded :excluded :admitted)\n                   :admission-reason\n                   (or excluded\n                       \"Guest source and explicit immutable context adapters over data/* and the declared kind/* host seams.\"))))\n        (edn/read-string (slurp \"test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& _]\n  (write-table! \"test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\"\n                \";; GENERATED admission inventory; each binding is :admitted or :excluded with a reason.\\n\"\n                (admission-rows))\n  (write-table! \"test/yang/latte_oracle/throw_sites.edn\"\n                (str \";; GENERATED from the manifest forms by yang.latte-oracle-test/throw-site-rows.\\n\"\n                     \";; One row per throw symbol; disposition :fixture | :deferred | :excluded.\\n\")\n                (derived 'throw-site-rows))\n  (write-table! \"test/yang/latte_oracle/case_arms.edn\"\n                (str \";; GENERATED from the manifest forms by yang.latte-oracle-test/case-arm-rows.\\n\"\n                     \";; One row per case site: each arm's clause constants, and whether it has a default.\\n\")\n                (derived 'case-arm-rows))\n  (shutdown-agents))\nmuse: workspace root: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3 (cwd default)\nmuse: workspace trust: trusted source=run-flag\nmuse: warning: rules file at /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/CLAUDE.md is ignored this session because AGENTS.md takes precedence in that directory; merge still-applicable guidance into AGENTS.md or remove one of the two files\nmuse: Skills: 38 loaded · 1 warning\nmuse:   `skills_catalog` was trimmed to fit its size limit (32 KB): 2 descriptions compacted, 0 skill ids omitted\nmuse:   Run `muse skills list --source all` for full diagnostics.\nmuse: retrying meta model stream in 1000ms (attempt 2/10)\nmuse: retrying meta model stream in 1000ms (attempt 2/10)\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-11 10:47:53 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 17:47:53 +07\n\nAll three r5 items are done, verified, and uncommitted (8 tracked files, +1620/−93).\n\n**F2 — caller threading:** [latte_oracle_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj) now allocates the run scope once per run via `fresh-admission-run` and threads it through `kernel-row`, `kernel-gate-evidence`, the proof-supply/proof-loop loops, and the principal binding test, with distinct ordinals per fixture and explicit scope+ordinal re-supply on replay. The new `test-cc3-caller-run-threads-distinct-admissions` pins distinctness through the actual `kernel-row` path (red first: unresolved `fresh-admission-run`).\n\n**F6 — maximum rule:** [the measurement script](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj) now judges by maximum sample, and the r4 findings table's binding-only verdict is corrected to EXCEEDED (8,044,024 B sample; samples unchanged).\n\n**V2 bounded run:** declared before running in [the v2 declaration](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md) (retained ceiling 12,000,000 B, +33.2% over the pilot compiled-inclusive maximum), preserving the superseded run as failed. V2 results, all max-based PASS: compiled-inclusive max 8,931,952 B / 12,000,000 B; peak heap max 283,147,736 B / 1 GiB; elapsed max 873 ms / 10,000 ms; all C lanes completed.\n\nVerification: 10 affected oracle deftests (230 assertions), gate evidence (2 tests, 1,301 assertions, `:gate-status :pass`), callsite battery (36/403), semantic nets (51/7,333), REPL nets (79/400), kondo 0 errors — all green.\n\nDeliverable is the worktree mirror at [the r5 findings](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md), since the canonical `datomworld/collab` path is outside this session's writable workspace; the v2 declaration is mirrored beside it. Nothing was committed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"