opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\n           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\n           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\n           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\n           ;; are selected away by :jolt reader branches, never loaded). No\n           ;; generated Java parser classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no\n           ;; dependency coordinate is fetched until a jolt-loaded namespace\n           ;; needs one.\n           :jolt {:replace-paths [\"src/jolt\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/clj\"]\n                  :replace-deps {}}\n           :jolt-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           ;; composed after :jolt (-M:jolt:jolt-test): the oracle tests and\n           ;; src/dev (src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj and its sentinel)\n           :jolt-test {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]}\n           ;; DIAGNOSTIC only (-M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test): a jolt stand-in\n           ;; for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures, whose root must\n           ;; precede test (src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc);\n           ;; jolt puts :extra-paths roots first, in alias order (-Spath)\n           :jolt-diag {:extra-paths [\"src/dev/jolt_diag\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.node-runner\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\n           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n M src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc\n M test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\n M test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\n M test/yin/vm/semantic/derive_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic/linearize_test.cljc\n?? CC3-REVIEW-R2.md\n?? CC3-REVIEW-R3.md\n?? CC3-REVIEW-R4.md\n?? CC3-REVIEW-R5.md\n?? CC3-REVIEW.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794374077000-engineer-cc3-fix-r2.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794376197000-engineer-cc3-fix-r3.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-engineer-cc3-fix-r4.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git ls-files test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj; sed -n '1,85p' test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj; sed -n '1,48p' test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj; nl -ba collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md | sed -n '1,155p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git ls-files test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj; sed -n '1,85p' test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj; sed -n '1,48p' test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj; nl -ba collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md | sed -n '1,155p'\"","aggregated_output":"test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj\ntest/d2_wedge_probe2.clj\n(ns d2-wedge-min-repro\n  \"The minimized reproduction of the H3-1 'wedge' — which is a false\n  negative, not a cycle.\n\n  What round 1 measured as 'the evaluator session terminates': a probe that\n  built `semantic/create-vm` + `tu/make-observer-session` and called\n  `observer/run-on-stream` — but never appended the fixture to the session\n  medium (no `tu/queue-rows!`). An observer session over an empty medium\n  loads nothing and runs nothing, and a fresh SemanticVM is `:halted? true`\n  before any program (yin.vm.semantic/create-vm mints `:halted? true`), so\n  the probe read 'halted, zero budget spent' off a machine that never\n  executed an instruction.\n\n  This file is the A/B/C pair that isolates it, each arm runnable alone:\n\n    arm A  reproduces round 1's drive exactly — 0 steps, halted=true,\n           the false negative in three lines\n    arm B  adds the ONE missing line (tu/queue-rows!) and drives the same\n           D2-compiled fixture through the same evaluator session: it\n           completes under the 2M budget with the correct outcome —\n           there is no non-terminating cycle in the evaluator session,\n           the observer coordination, or any encoder layer\n    arm C  shrinks the budget to 10000 steps and shows run-bounded's\n           exhaustion throw PROPAGATES out of observer/run-on-stream\n           (carry-session rethrows; it never feeds the loop), carrying\n           the advanced machine under :consumer and the partial session\n           under :session — the opt-in recovery data, not a retry cycle.\n\n  The kernel-c semantic path (`run-guest-machine`) has no encoder session\n  in it at any commit: it is tu/make-observer-session + tu/queue-rows! +\n  observer/run-on-stream, single stage. The two C lanes differ only in\n  machine construction and loader.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n            [yang.latte-oracle-test :as latte]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n(def ^:private original-step vm/step)\n(def steps (atom 0))\n\n(defn- counted-step\n  [machine]\n  (swap! steps inc)\n  (original-step machine))\n\n(defn- fixture-ast\n  \"The D2-compiled check-assume-have-discharge fixture, as kernel-c sees it.\"\n  []\n  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)]\n    (when-not (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n      (throw (ex-info \"fixture no longer compiles\" {:status (:status compiled)})))\n    (:ast compiled)))\n\n(defn- load-rows\n  []\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader\n    (fn [m rows stamp]\n      (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n      (semantic/load-vector m\n                            (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n                            vm/semantic-contract))\n    vm/ast-contract))\n\n(defn- bounded-run\n  \"run-guest-machine's runner, verbatim.\"\n  [step-limit]\n  (fn [machine]\n    (loop [v machine n 0]\n      (cond\n        (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\n        (= n step-limit) (throw (ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"\n                                         {:lane :semantic :steps n :consumer v}))\n        :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc n))))))\n\n(defn- bounded [x]\n  (let [s (pr-str x)]\n    (if (> (count s) 200) (subs s 0 200) s)))\n(ns d2-wedge-probe2\n  \"H3-1 wedge diagnostic, round 2: drive the REAL kernel-c semantic path.\n\n  Round 1's probe (test/d2_wedge_probe.clj) never queued the fixture onto\n  the session medium — `tu/make-observer-session` mints an EMPTY medium and\n  the probe called no queue variant — so its evaluator-session drive was\n  vacuous: a fresh SemanticVM is `:halted? true` (yin.vm.semantic/create-vm)\n  before any step, and run-on-stream over an empty medium loads nothing and\n  runs nothing. Stage A below reproduces that drive and measures its step\n  count to confirm the false negative.\n\n  Stage B re-measures the exact kernel-c semantic path —\n  `yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine`'s semantic branch\n  (tu/make-observer-session + tu/queue-rows! + observer/run-on-stream +\n  run-bounded over vm/step) — instrumented at vm/step (count, wall time,\n  machine entering each step) and at the run-on-stream boundary (ready\n  checks, batches loaded, run entries with per-run step deltas), with a\n  watchdog that separates the three failure shapes:\n\n    - BUDGET-THROWN   run-bounded's 2M exhaustion throw reaches the caller\n    - WEDGE-IN-STEP   step count frozen: one vm/step never returns; the\n                      worker stack trace plus the entering machine are dumped\n    - RATE-COLLAPSE   steps still advance but steps/sec decays toward zero;\n                      the per-tick rate table plus a final snapshot are dumped\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n            [yang.latte-oracle-test :as latte]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n(def ^:private original-step vm/step)\n(def ^:private original-run-on-stream observer/run-on-stream)\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- instrumentation\n\n(def steps (atom 0))\n(def in-step-nanos (atom 0))\n(def recent-durations (atom []))          ;; last 64 step durations, nanos\n(def last-machine (volatile! nil))        ;; machine entering the latest step\n(def load-count (atom 0))\n(def ready-count (atom 0))\n(def run-log (atom []))                   ;; one entry per run-on-stream `run`\n(def start-ms (atom nil))\n     1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-11 13:40:00 GMT\n     2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 20:40:00 +0700\n     3\tCoding-Agent: muse\n     4\tSession-ID: 7db9b5cc-3472-4c31-9657-1b41aaa76ae3\n     5\t\n     6\t# cc3 bounded run declaration v2 — NEW versioned run (astra r4 ruling (c))\n     7\t\n     8\tThis declaration is written BEFORE the v2 measurement run, per design\n     9\t§6.3 and astra's r4 exceedance ruling (c). It creates a NEW, explicitly\n    10\tversioned bounded run. It does not amend, re-scope, or relabel the\n    11\tsuperseded run (see §5).\n    12\t\n    13\t## 1. Pinned corpus, revision, host, and JVM settings\n    14\t\n    15\t| Item | Pinned value |\n    16\t|---|---|\n    17\t| Worktree / branch | `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`, branch `cc3-lowering-provenance` |\n    18\t| Base revision | `ced9f2c2bdb43ab4a416b4ab408c76eb29245764` plus the uncommitted eight-file cc3 diff (+1495/−68 at r4 delivery; latte oracle test file further changed in r5 for F2 caller threading — behaviour-neutral for this fixture's compiled content) |\n    19\t| Fixture (the whole corpus of this run) | `{:id :cc3-binding :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` admitted through `kernel-compile`, bound through `cc3-oracle-binding` |\n    20\t| Upstream oracle revision | latte-kernel `86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279` (pinned in `deps.edn` `:test` alias) |\n    21\t| Compiler base recorded by the evidence harness | `7dc18478` |\n    22\t| Host | Darwin 25.6.0 arm64, Apple M1 Pro, 17,179,869,184 B RAM |\n    23\t| JVM | OpenJDK 17.0.18+0 (Homebrew, 64-Bit Server VM, mixed mode) |\n    24\t| Clojure | Clojure CLI 1.12.4.1602; project `:test` JVM opts `-Xss64m`, no explicit `-Xmx` (JVM default max heap) |\n    25\t| Measurement script | `collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj` (in-repo, r5 revision: maximum-based rule, compiled-inclusive holder) |\n    26\t\n    27\t## 2. Retained object set and maximum simultaneous retention\n    28\t\n    29\tThe retained set for one fixture, all held simultaneously by one local\n    30\tholder (never a global Var), is:\n    31\t\n    32\t- the **compiled input**: the `kernel-compile` result (compiled AST,\n    33\t  stamped AST, site table, retained `:admission-origin`);\n    34\t- the **binding**: `cc3-oracle-binding` result (C1 tree, rows, marked\n    35\t  and eligible occurrence sets, site→key binding);\n    36\t- the **reconstruction evidence**: the binding's stamped tree/rows,\n    37\t  stamped marked/eligible sets, site correspondence map, and stamped\n    38\t  paths — i.e. everything needed to reconstruct and verify each bound\n    39\t  key from the retained compilation;\n    40\t- the lowered images: `linearize/project-rows` output plus\n    41\t  `derive/stack-image` and `derive/register-image`;\n    42\t- the provenance relation (schema-1 map over admission/root and the\n    43\t  semantic, stack, and register call-provenance) and, in the pipeline\n    44\t  variant, its durable record in a file-backed content store.\n    45\t\n    46\tTwo holder variants are measured: **binding-only** (binding, lowered\n    47\timages, relation, reconstruction evidence — the compiled input is\n    48\treleased after binding) and **compiled-inclusive** (the same set plus\n    49\tthe retained compiled input). The compiled-inclusive variant is the\n    50\tacceptance variant; the binding-only variant is reported for\n    51\tcomparison and is NOT the acceptance holder.\n    52\t\n    53\t**Maximum simultaneously retained fixtures: 1.** Every retained and\n    54\tpeak measurement holds exactly one fixture's retained set at a time;\n    55\tthe previous holder is released (and GC-pinned) before the next\n    56\trepetition builds a new one.\n    57\t\n    58\t## 3. Ceilings (separate, finite, pilot-justified)\n    59\t\n    60\tPilot measurements (superseded run, r4, warm JVM, same host/JVM):\n    61\tbinding-only retained samples 7,960,192 / 7,921,728 / 8,044,024 B\n    62\t(median 7,960,192 B, **maximum 8,044,024 B**); compiled-inclusive\n    63\tsamples 9,008,912 / 8,939,024 / 8,826,416 B (median 8,939,024 B,\n    64\t**maximum 9,008,912 B**); serialized rows 293,924 B; serialized\n    65\trelation 802,260 B; peak used heap 292,720,240 B (GC-pinned baseline\n    66\t38,967,336 B); pipeline elapsed 1,727 ms.\n    67\t\n    68\t| Ceiling | v2 bound | Justification / headroom over pilot |\n    69\t|---|---|---|\n    70\t| Storage, per artifact (serialized canonical bytes) | **2,000,000 B** | Kept from r2. Pilot rows 293,924 B (6.8× headroom), relation 802,260 B (2.5× headroom). |\n    71\t| Storage, aggregate retained serialized set (rows + relation + durable record, 1 fixture) | **4,000,000 B** | Pilot rows+relation = 1,096,184 B; the durable record is a small map over the same data. 4,000,000 B is ≥3.6× the pilot partial sum, leaving room for the record while staying finite. |\n    72\t| Retained memory, aggregate (1 fixture, compiled-inclusive holder) | **12,000,000 B** | Set ABOVE the pilot compiled-inclusive **maximum** 9,008,912 B by 2,991,088 B (**+33.2% headroom**; +34.2% over the 8,939,024 B median; +49.2% over the binding-only maximum 8,044,024 B). Pilot repetition spread was ~2% (8,826,416–9,008,912 B), so 33% covers GC-delta noise, the longer r5 run-scope strings (tens of bytes), and host jitter on this machine class, without being an order-of-magnitude loosening. The floor is the measured maximum, per ruling (c): a ceiling at or below 9,008,912 B would declare a run already known to exceed it. |\n    73\t| Peak heap (absolute used heap during the pipeline) | **1,073,741,824 B (1 GiB)** | Kept from r2. Pilot peak 292,720,240 B is 27.3% of this ceiling (3.67× headroom); the figure is absolute used heap (baseline + harness + transients), so the margin absorbs sampler/baseline variance. |\n    74\t| Time, per pipeline repetition (compile → persistence → both tagged lanes) | **10,000 ms** | Kept from r2. Pilot 1,727 ms gives 5.8× headroom; warm-JVM figure, cold-JVM limits are stated in §4. |\n    75\t| Guest instructions / trace records per C lane | **4,000,000 / 1,000,000** | Restated from the r1 record, NOT raised. |\n    76\t\n    77\t## 4. Exact reproducible measurement procedure\n    78\t\n    79\tScript: `collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj`\n    80\t(r5 revision). Run from the worktree root:\n    81\t\n    82\t```\n    83\tclojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:f6 {:extra-paths [\"test\"] :extra-deps {latte-kernel/latte-kernel {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\" :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}}}}' -M:f6 collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj\n    84\t```\n    85\t\n    86\t(the latte-kernel git dependency is named explicitly because the\n    87\tproject's `:test` alias, which normally carries it, also carries the\n    88\ttest-runner main opts; the git checkout is already cached locally.\n    89\tVerdicts are read from the script's printed `:under-ceilings-v2` map,\n    90\tcomputed by the maximum rule below.)\n    91\t\n    92\tProcedure, in order:\n    93\t\n    94\t1. **Warmup**: build one retained structure and one full pipeline\n    95\t   pass, DISCARD both, GC-pin. Class loading / JIT are charged to the\n    96\t   warmup, not to measured repetitions.\n    97\t2. **Retained memory**: 5 repetitions per holder variant\n    98\t   (binding-only, then compiled-inclusive). Each repetition builds a\n    99\t   fresh holder held only by a local, samples GC-pinned used heap\n   100\t   (`System/gc()`, 50 ms, `System/gc()`, then\n   101\t   `Runtime.totalMemory − freeMemory`) before and after, uses\n   102\t   `System/identityHashCode` on the holder AFTER the second sample so\n   103\t   it cannot be collected early, and releases it on return. ALL 5\n   104\t   samples per variant are recorded.\n   105\t3. **Peak / pipeline**: 3 pipeline repetitions. A sampler thread\n   106\t   records used heap every 2 ms across lowering → binding /\n   107\t   projection / derives → actual serialization\n   108\t   (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) → durable persistence\n   109\t   (`dao.jing/materialize!` of relation and record into a file-backed\n   110\t   `yin.repl.store`, closed) → tagged execution (both C lanes must\n   111\t   reach `:completed`). Peak, per-repetition elapsed time, and\n   112\t   serialized byte counts are recorded per repetition.\n   113\t4. **Pass/fail is MAXIMUM-based** (r5 F6 fix): a ceiling is met only\n   114\t   if the MAXIMUM observed value is at or under it — retained memory:\n   115\t   max of the 5 compiled-inclusive samples ≤ 12,000,000 B (the\n   116\t   binding-only samples are reported, and also max-checked against\n   117\t   the same aggregate ceiling for information); storage: max per\n   118\t   artifact and max aggregate ≤ their ceilings; peak heap: max peak\n   119\t   over the 3 repetitions ≤ 1 GiB; time: max elapsed ≤ 10,000 ms.\n   120\t   Any single sample over its ceiling = EXCEEDED. Medians are\n   121\t   printed for information only and never establish compliance.\n   122\t\n   123\tSampling limitations (named, not hidden): retained and peak figures\n   124\tare process-wide JVM used-heap values, not an object-graph census;\n   125\t`System/gc()` is a hint the JVM honored observably here, not a\n   126\tguarantee; 2 ms peak sampling can miss sub-2 ms transients; figures\n   127\tare comparable only on this host/JVM class and only for the named\n   128\tholder scope; times are warm-JVM (the discarded warmup precedes all\n   129\tmeasured repetitions).\n   130\t\n   131\t## 5. Superseded run: failed status preserved\n   132\t\n   133\tThe r2/r4 bounded run (8,000,000 B aggregate retained ceiling,\n   134\tmedian-based accounting in its r4 record) **FAILED and remains\n   135\tfailed**. Its exceedances, restated with maximum-based accounting:\n   136\t\n   137\t- compiled-inclusive holder: samples 9,008,912 / 8,939,024 /\n   138\t  8,826,416 B — every sample over the 8,000,000 B ceiling.\n   139\t  **EXCEEDED.**\n   140\t- binding-only holder: samples 7,960,192 / 7,921,728 / 8,044,024 B —\n   141\t  the 8,044,024 B sample is over the 8,000,000 B ceiling, so under\n   142\t  the corrected maximum rule this holder is **EXCEEDED** too (its r4\n   143\t  \"under (99.5%)\" median label is corrected in r5; the samples\n   144\t  themselves are unchanged).\n   145\t\n   146\tNothing in this v2 declaration relabels that run successful, raises\n   147\tits ceiling retroactively, or shrinks its fixture. The v2 run below\n   148\tis a separate, new run under the ceilings in §3; its results are\n   149\trecorded in the r5 findings, not back-written into the superseded\n   150\trun's record.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
