as plain data\n    31\t  (`\"<label>-<UUID>\"`) plus a run-local ordinal allocator (an atom\n    32\t  created per run, held only by the run map; no per-JVM global\n    33\t  counter). `kernel-compile-in-run` / `kernel-row-in-run` thread that\n    34\t  run through the actual callers, assigning DISTINCT ordinals within\n    35\t  the run. Replay never allocates a fresh run: it explicitly\n    36\t  re-supplies the retained run's scope+ordinal, or reuses the\n    37\t  retained compilation (the pre-existing binding-replay pin).\n    38\t- `kernel-row` now takes `[fixture run-scope admission-ordinal]`\n    39\t  (the old always-`:kernel-row 0` call is gone) and records\n    40\t  `:admission-origin` / `:admission-scope` / `:admission-ordinal` on\n    41\t  the row; the evidence writer dissocs those three when landing the\n    42\t  versioned evidence file, so generated evidence stays stable across\n    43\t  fresh scopes. `kernel-gate-evidence` — the run composition of the\n    44\t  evidence run — allocates its scope ONCE and threads it through\n    45\t  every fixture row via `kernel-row-in-run`.\n    46\t- Every other caller updated: the proof-supply doseq, the proof-loop\n    47\t  doseq, and check-proof (one `fresh-admission-run` per testing\n    48\t  block, distinct ordinals per iteration); the principal binding\n    49\t  test (allocates its enclosing `:cc3-binding-run` identity once,\n    50\t  compiles as its ordinal-0 admission, and pins\n    51\t  `[(:scope run) 0]` as the origin's batch token); the duplicate-id\n    52\t  test; `test-kernel-unused-arity-execution`; the h3-2 and h3-3\n    53\t  families; and the attribution battery (one run threaded through\n    54\t  all its rows, including the nested case-3/case-6 rows). No\n    55\t  `:kernel-row 0`, `:proof-* 0`, `:check-proof 0`, or fixed\n    56\t  `:cc3-binding-run 0` coordinate remains.\n    57\t- Pin through the ACTUAL caller path (new deftest\n    58\t  `test-cc3-caller-run-threads-distinct-admis